  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Every year, over 3 million people in the United States are diagnosed with
    a herniated disk. \n\nSpinal disks are located between the spinal verebrae. Herniation
    occurs when a disk tears and the central \"nucleus pulposus\" leaks through the
    tear, compressing the spinal nerve root and causing pain. \n\nCommon symptoms:
    back pain, neck pain, numbness or tingling in arms and legs, and muscle weakness.
    \n\nCommon causes: aging, traumatic injuries, and improper lifting. \n\nCommon
    risk factors: smoking, sitting or driving for long periods of time, being overweight,
    and having a connective tissue disorder. \n\nTreatment options: Medication, physical
    therapy, spinal injections, and surgery, such as a diskectomy*.\n\n*A diskectomy
    is a procedure where part of the herniated disk is removed and has an overall
    success rate of 60% to 90%. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2d3a3b352dc20b9408ce17d372ee7d44, type: 2}
